        {
          "id": "l10",
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "text": "And here is the catch: the Bajau, sea nomads of Southeast Asia, have already grown a *bigger* tank.",
          "pauseAfterMs": 500
        },
        {
          "id": "l11",
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "text": "Their divers spend up to sixty percent of a working day diving for *fish*.",
          "pauseAfterMs": 500
        },
        {
          "id": "l12",
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "text": "Scientists scanned the spleens of the Bajau and of their farming neighbours, the *Saluan*.",
          "pauseAfterMs": 500
        },
        {
          "id": "l13",
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "text": "The Bajau spleen was about fifty percent *bigger*, roughly the size of a tennis ball.",
          "pauseAfterMs": 500
        },
        {
          "id": "l14",
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "text": "It was big even in Bajau who do not dive, so it is in their *genes*.",
          "pauseAfterMs": 500
        },
        {
          "id": "l15",
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "text": "Scientists think it took only around a thousand years at sea, a *blink* for evolution.",
          "pauseAfterMs": 1100
        }
